<!-- ============ 1. INTRODUCTION ============ -->
<h1>1. Introduction</h1>
<p>This document describes the work I have done for Lab 3 of CS344: Web Engineering. In this lab, I was required to take my existing portfolio website from Lab 2 and improve it significantly. The main focus was on moving all the CSS styling into a separate external file, organizing the project files into proper folders, using CSS float and clear properties for layouts, and finally deploying the website on GitHub Pages so it can be accessed online by anyone.</p>

<p>My portfolio website has five pages in total. There is a Home page that talks about me and my background, a Hobbies page where I have listed the activities I enjoy doing in my free time, a Skills page that shows my programming abilities and spoken languages, a Gallery page with multiple photos arranged in a grid, and a Contact page where I have given my details and also placed a simple message form.</p>

<p>The key difference from Lab 2 is that now the website looks much more polished and consistent. Earlier, each page had its own CSS written inside the HTML file itself, and the styling was not the same everywhere. In this version, I have created one single stylesheet that all pages share, which makes the whole site feel unified and properly designed.</p>


<!-- ============ 2. OBJECTIVES ============ -->
<h1>2. Objectives of the Lab</h1>
<p>The following were the main objectives I aimed to achieve in this lab:</p>
<ul>
    <li>Move all CSS code from inside the HTML pages to a single external stylesheet called <strong>style.css</strong>, and link it to every page.</li>
    <li>Organize the project properly by keeping CSS files in a <strong>css/</strong> folder and all images in an <strong>images/</strong> folder.</li>
    <li>Use the CSS <strong>float</strong> property to arrange content side by side, such as placing text next to images and creating multi-column card layouts.</li>
    <li>Use the CSS <strong>clear</strong> property to fix layout issues that come from floated elements.</li>
    <li>Style the navigation bar so all the links appear horizontally in a single row across every page.</li>
    <li>Build an image gallery with multiple photos aligned using float and clear.</li>
    <li>Upload the entire project to a GitHub repository and enable GitHub Pages so the site is live on the internet.</li>
</ul>


